# Copy this file to .env (same folder) and fill in your own values from your
# Microsoft Foundry project. .env is for your machine only -- never commit it
# and never paste its actual values into chat with anyone, including Claude.
#
# Where to find these -- in your Foundry project, go to Deployments, click
# your chat model deployment (e.g. gpt-5.6-luna), and its detail panel shows
# all three:
#   - AZURE_OPENAI_ENDPOINT: the "Project endpoint" panel's Python code
#     sample shows an `endpoint` value ending in .services.ai.azure.com --
#     that's NOT this one. Use the resource's v1 API endpoint instead:
#     https://<your-resource-name>.openai.azure.com/openai/v1/
#     (same resource name, different host+path -- must end in /openai/v1/).
#     This project's chat model (agent/config.py) uses the newer v1 API
#     surface, which is plain OpenAI-API-compatible and doesn't need an
#     api-version parameter at all -- no AZURE_OPENAI_API_VERSION here.
#   - AZURE_OPENAI_API_KEY: shown (masked, with a reveal icon) right on that
#     same deployment detail panel.
#   - AZURE_OPENAI_CHAT_DEPLOYMENT: the deployment name shown at the top of
#     that panel (e.g. "gpt-5.6-luna") -- not the underlying model version.

AZURE_OPENAI_ENDPOINT=https://your-resource-name.openai.azure.com/openai/v1/
AZURE_OPENAI_API_KEY=your-api-key-here
AZURE_OPENAI_CHAT_DEPLOYMENT=your-chat-deployment-name
